## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about battery UX, scheduling, and real-world validation with a beginner feature.

## Key Concepts
- On-device scheduling
- Battery/CPU energy estimation
- Telemetry and privacy constraints
- Rollout strategy and break-even analysis
- UX impact

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldBatch(now, lastSent, urgency, dnd) {
  if (urgency === 'urgent') return false;
  if (dnd) return true;
  const withinWindow = (now - lastSent) < 15*60*1000;
  return withinWindow;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate energy savings in production?
- How would you handle edge cases like user toggling DND mid-window?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a feature into a concrete CBA with privacy constraints, rollout strategy, and measurable ROI.

## Key Concepts

- On-device perceptual hashing
- Memory and CPU budgeting for fingerprint indices
- Data savings vs latency trade-offs
- Privacy/compliance, consent flows
- Rollout plans, offline fallback, drift maintenance, ROI calculation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: fingerprint a media item and decide upload
function shouldUpload(media) {
  const fp = perceptualFingerprint(media);
  const exists = fingerprintIndex.has(fp);
  if (exists) return false;
  fingerprintIndex.add(fp);
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and validate data savings at scale?
